MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The headphones fit my listening and desk setup, especially after buying a headphone mount. I would explore the Jabra pair first because wireless listening and noise cancellation add useful capabilities.",
    "The ergonomic keyboard connects to my interest in typing comfort, while the USB flash drive offers a practical way to move files alongside my existing memory cards and computer accessories."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The iPad protector requires a device I have not shown I own; my Kindle does not make that accessory useful to me. Similarly, a GPS-compatible memory card does not establish an interest in a Garmin fitness tracker.",
    "The rugged camera, studio boom and surveillance camera serve projects I have not shown a need for. The router is closer to my networking interests, but buying Ethernet accessories does not mean I need to replace my router."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in electronics seems to have been stretched into interest in unrelated photography, surveillance and fitness equipment.",
    "Shared names or connections seem to carry too much weight: Garmin storage compatibility does not imply fitness interest, and wired networking accessories do not imply a router upgrade."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent accessories point toward maintaining and organizing a computer workspace: cable management, wired connections, cleaning equipment and headphone storage. Items that help with those tasks feel more relevant.",
    "A useful addition needs either to work with equipment I already have or offer a clear improvement, such as quieter listening, typing comfort or portable storage. Frequent accessory purchases do not mean I currently need every related device."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "You recognized my interest in practical computer accessories, but extended it to devices and projects that my recent activity does not support."
}
